      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "Brachialis is the prime elbow flexor in all forearm positions because it inserts on the ulna and so is unaffected by pronation or supination. It crosses no other joint in the vocabulary, so it has no shoulder, grip or wrist role.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
