        {
          "demand": "shoulder_position_hold",
          "weight": 0.3
        }
      ],
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "Coracobrachialis is a weak synergist for shoulder flexion and adduction and assists horizontal adduction. It helps resist inferior displacement of the humeral head, and as an isometric shoulder flexor/adductor it assists the anterior deltoid in holding the upper arm beside the torso against the shoulder-extension moment of a curl. It does not cross the elbow, so it has no elbow action.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
