      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "Shared with the short head, this is a major elbow flexor, strongest with the forearm supinated. It is also a major supinator, most effective with the elbow flexed. Its intra-articular tendon weakly assists shoulder flexion and, with the humerus externally rotated, abduction, and it helps depress and centre the humeral head.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
