          "weight": 0.3
        }
      ],
      "stabilizes": [],
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The long head is a major elbow extender and the only triceps head that crosses the shoulder; it assists shoulder extension mainly from a flexed position, and also assists adduction. Its glenohumeral_stabilization role was removed: its support of the inferior capsule in abduction is passive and minor, it does not centre the humeral head like the rotator cuff, and in curls it acts as an antagonist rather than a stabilizer.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
      "base_id": "muscle.medial_head_of_triceps_brachii",
      "movement_muscle": true,
